   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the Mount Olivet Baptist Church to file an application for a real property tax exemption",
    "basePrintNo": "S5763",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5763-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5763\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to authorize the Mount Olivet Baptist Church to file an\napplication for a real property tax exemption\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo allow a retroactive application for real property tax exemption for\nthe Mount Olivet Baptist Church, for certain real property owned in\nthe City of Peekskill, Westchester County.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of this legislation would authorize the Assessor of the City\nof Peekskill to accept an application, from Mount Olivet Baptist\nChurch, for exemption from real property taxes pursuant to Section\n420-a of the Real Property Tax Law for the 2008-2009 assessment roll\nfor the parcel owned by the Church, located in the City of Peekskill\nat 1432 Park Street.\n\nIf accepted, the application shall be reviewed as if it had been\nreceived on or before the taxable status date established for such\nrolls.\n\nIf satisfied that the Mount Olivet Baptist Church would otherwise have\nbeen entitled to said exemption by the appropriate taxable status\ndates, the Assessor may, upon approval of the Peekskill City Council,\ngrant exemption from taxation based on the 2008-2009 assessment roll,\nand owing by such Church on the effective date of this act, and make\nappropriate correction of the subject rolls.\n\nIf such exemption is granted and the Church has paid any tax with\nrespect to the subject rolls, the governing body or tax department may\nprovide for a refund or cancel all remaining unpaid taxes, interest,\nrelated fines and penalties.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Mount Olivet Baptist Church is seeking an exemption of taxes from\nthe date of purchase of premises located at 1432 Park Street,\nPeekskill, New York.\n\nThis legislation would authorize the Assessor of the City of\nPeekskill, upon approval of the City Council of Peekskill, to grant\nthe exemption from taxation beginning with the date of acquisition of\nthe property by Mount Olivet Baptist Church and make the appropriate\ncorrections to the applicable tax roll.\n\nIt is intended by this bill to ameliorate the hardship that will be\nsuffered by the Mount Olivet Baptist Church, a charitable entity under\n§420-a of the Real Property Tax Law, if it is required to pay the\nproperty taxes due as described above.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act would take effect immediately.\n",
